37":109,"_39":110,"_41":108,"_43":67,"_45":67,"_47":111,"_49":50,"_51":112,"_53":113,"_55":114,"_57":115,"_58":116,"_60":117,"_62":118,"_64":119,"_66":67,"_68":69},{"_25":82,"_27":83,"_29":84,"_31":85,"_33":86,"_35":87,"_37":67,"_39":67,"_41":88,"_43":67,"_45":67,"_47":89,"_49":48,"_51":90,"_53":91,"_55":92,"_57":93,"_58":94,"_60":95,"_62":96,"_64":97,"_66":67,"_68":69},{"_25":26,"_27":28,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":42,"_43":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":56,"_57":-5,"_58":59,"_60":61,"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67,"_68":69},"id","898","name","Joaquim Nabuco","type","person","startDescription","A Brazilian statesman, abolitionist, and diplomat, he was a leading figure in the fight against slavery in Brazil and advocated for social reforms.","endDescription","His efforts contributed significantly to the abolition of slavery in Brazil and his influence is still felt in Brazilian society.","startYear",1849,"startMonth",8,"startDay",3,"endYear",1910,"endMonth",1,"endDay",17,"startSignificance",0.7,"endSignificance",0.8,"imageUrl","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ambassador_joaquim_nabuco_in_court_dress.jpg/330px-Ambassador_joaquim_nabuco_in_court_dress.jpg","imageCredit","Image: Joaquim Nabuco / Wikimedia Commons","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joaquim_Nabuco","cdnId","country",{"_27":79,"_80":81},"subjects",[76],"group",{"_27":73,"_74":75},"user",{"_25":70,"_71":72},"likes",0,"liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Colonial and Imperial Brazil","icon","GiBrazilFlag",{"_25":77,"_27":78},"2","politics","Brazil","continent","SouthAmerica","615","Brazilian Golden Age","period","A flourishing period in Brazilian history marked by economic growth, cultural development, and political stability.","The era concluded with the establishment of the republic, leading to significant changes in governance and society.",1840,1889,0.75,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Constru%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Ponte_Rio-Niter%C3%B3i.tif/lossy-page1-320px-Constru%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Ponte_Rio-Niter%C3%B3i.tif.jpg","Arquivo Nacional / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Golden_Age","images/43a8fab2797693b6a5b60844700301daa01678cb.webp",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[100],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":98,"_71":99},"7","Kushim",{"_25":101,"_27":102},"8","economic","577","Independence of Brazil","event","A pivotal moment when Brazil declared its independence from Portuguese rule, marking the beginning of a new era for the nation.","This declaration led to the establishment of Brazil as an independent empire, significantly altering its political landscape.",1822,9,7,0.9,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Pedro_Am%C3%A9rico_-_Independ%C3%AAncia_ou_Morte_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-Pedro_Am%C3%A9rico_-_Independ%C3%AAncia_ou_Morte_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","Pedro Américo / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence_of_Brazil","images/5e190ad008306014b42c3bc00570b1c6d06f2446.webp",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[120],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":77,"_27":78},"581","Brazilian Empire","A significant period marked by the establishment of a constitutional monarchy following Brazil's independence.","The empire ended with the proclamation of the republic, leading to major political changes in the country.",0.85,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Flag_of_Brazil_%281853-1889%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Brazil_%281853-1889%29.svg.png","Empire of Brazil / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Empire","images/2b8cff392a98d5945398992cc78578bcd586492e.webp",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[134],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":77,"_27":78},"1683","Cultural Revolution of the 19th Century","A transformative era marked by the emergence of new artistic, literary, and philosophical movements in Brazil, influenced by European trends.","This period laid the groundwork for modern Brazilian culture and identity, reflecting a blend of indigenous, African, and European influences.",1800,1899,0.6,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Roda_de_capoeira4.jpg/330px-Roda_de_capoeira4.jpg","Image: Culture of Brazil / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_Brazil#19th_century",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[149,150],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":153,"_27":154},{"_25":151,"_27":152},"9","art","3","culture","1569","Dom Pedro I","A prominent figure in Brazilian history, he played a crucial role in the country's independence from Portugal and became its first emperor.","His reign ended with his abdication, leading to significant political changes in Brazil.",1798,10,12,1834,24,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/DpedroI-brasil-full.jpg/330px-DpedroI-brasil-full.jpg","Image: Pedro I of Brazil / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dom_Pedro_I_of_Brazil",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[171,172],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":173,"_27":174},{"_25":77,"_27":78},"1","military","1680","Inconfidência Mineira","An unsuccessful conspiracy aimed at achieving independence from Portuguese rule, led by a group of intellectuals and elites in Minas Gerais.","The movement was suppressed, and its leaders faced severe consequences, but it inspired future independence movements.",1789,1792,0.5,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Bandeira_da_Inconfid%C3%AAncia_1789_Os_Inconfidentes.jpg/330px-Bandeira_da_Inconfid%C3%AAncia_1789_Os_Inconfidentes.jpg","Image: Inconfidência Mineira / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inconfid%C3%AAncia_Mineira",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[189,190],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":77,"_27":78},{"_25":191,"_27":192},"4","intellectual","1682","War of the Emboabas","A conflict between Portuguese settlers and the native inhabitants over control of gold mining in the region of Minas Gerais.","The war concluded with the Treaty of Taubaté, which established peace and defined territorial rights.",1708,1709,0.4,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Guerra_dos_Emboabas.jpg/330px-Guerra_dos_Emboabas.jpg","Image: War of the Emboabas / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Emboabas",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[207,208],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":173,"_27":174},{"_25":101,"_27":102},"627","Brazilian Gold Rush","A significant economic boom in Brazil driven by the discovery of gold, leading to increased immigration and urbanization.","The rush ended as gold reserves diminished, leading to economic shifts and changes in population dynamics.",1690,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Rodolfo_Amoedo_-_Ciclo_do_Ouro%2C_Acervo_do_Museu_Paulista_da_USP.jpg/330px-Rodolfo_Amoedo_-_Ciclo_do_Ouro%2C_Acervo_do_Museu_Paulista_da_USP.jpg","Rodolfo Amoedo / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Gold_Rush","images/0ee0a7764f8bd6746236d2e49a85e872291b9021.webp",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[222],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":98,"_71":99},{"_25":101,"_27":102},"1681","Battle of Guararapes","A series of battles fought between Dutch colonial forces and Portuguese settlers in Brazil, pivotal in the struggle for control over the region.","The Portuguese victory solidified their control over northeastern Brazil and marked a turning point in the conflict with the Dutch.",1648,4,28,1649,"","Image: Battle of Guararapes / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guararapes",{"_27":79,"_80":81},[238,239],{"_27":73,"_74":75},{"_25":70,"_71":72},{"_25":173,"_27":174},{"_25":77,"_27":78},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true,30]
